{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqs6aze3yvt","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Grader runs ONLY in agentic subconscious search-context, not plain GET search — ON arm must use it for production fidelity","summary":"EMPIRICAL (verified in code): the LLM search-loop grader runs ONLY in the subconscious AGENTIC loop — store.searchContext() in lib/subconscious/index.js (~2629) loops compileSearchContext + calls gradeSearchRound per round, on defaultSubconsciousStore which is built with graderEnabled:true, exposed at POST /subconscious/search-context (routes/subconscious.js ~307-326). The plain GET /search route (routes/graph.js:101 -> lib/search/context-compiler.js) is ONE-SHOT and has ZERO grader references. CONSEQUENCES for the agent-memory memory bench: (a) the `search`/RAG arm (GET /search, gated=false) and the ON arm's old read (GET /search?task_key=) do NOT exercise the grader at all; (b) to make the ON arm BOTH grader-exercising AND byte-identical to the production agentic context-retrieval, it must read via /subconscious/search-context (task-gated DAG Tier-1 + graded RAG), same store/code path production uses. SEPARATELY: `enrich` is code_node-only (lib/code-extract/ingest.js enrichBody folds source body into code_node embeds) so it NEVER touches conversation-note ingestion — it has zero effect on this memory bench. The embedded bench daemon resolves a grader backend via .env.local CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN (loaded by lib/load-env.js). This is why a fresh memory-bench run on current main does NOT measure enrich/grader unless the ON arm is rewired to the agentic path.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-24T14:33:13.899Z","vec":[-0.07473372668027878,0.020748376846313477,-0.04405129328370094,0.0060551706701517105,0.029386263340711594,-0.056836873292922974,-0.017100222408771515,0.03777710348367691,0.026721257716417313,-0.030943548306822777,0.0071135456673800945,-0.0005052249762229621,0.037832111120224,-0.04109147563576698,0.05141326785